{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments ["<b>לשוח בשדה</b> — this means that Isaac established the Minhah prayer, and then Rebecca happened to come to him. This is what is written: 'For this shall every godly one pray to You at a time of finding' (Psalms 32:6) — that is, a wife, as it is written: 'He who finds a wife finds good' (Proverbs 18:22)." "<b> לפנות ערב</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other: והיה לפנות ערב ירחץ במים — a hint to what the Sages said: they immerse from Minhah and onward. For just as here it is Minhah, which Isaac established as the Minhah prayer, so too there it is Minhah."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:53.712176583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}